# The races that ThreadSanitizer reports inside the libraries that the
# port links uninstrumented: SDL3 and FluidSynth run their own threads,
# FluidSynth renders through OpenMP (libgomp), and SDL3 reaches D-Bus,
# whose locks the sanitizer sees in part. race_top matches the access's
# own frame, so that a race of src/sys's audio callbacks, which run
# under SDL3's threads, stays reported. libgomp and Mesa's libgallium,
# which SDL3's renderer loads, allocate and free in their own threads,
# under barriers and locks of their own: called_from_lib passes over
# their calls of malloc and free. bin/headless reads this file.
race_top:libSDL3.so
deadlock:libSDL3.so
race_top:libfluidsynth.so
deadlock:libfluidsynth.so
race_top:libgomp.so
deadlock:libgomp.so
race_top:libdbus-1.so
deadlock:libdbus-1.so
called_from_lib:libgallium
called_from_lib:libgomp.so
